So I downloaded it and gave it a try, albeit not in a real game --
I started in wizard mode and wished up a set of equipment that is
typical of my mid-Gehennom characters.  (Anyone who doesn't want
more spoilers on the branch, don't read this.)

Some random notes:

- The new levels are an interesting change.  I navigated them mostly
  with a couple wands of fire and water walking boots.
- It would be nice to have a message when entering Sheol (like
  "The heat and smoke are gone.") -- I did notice that there was
  an appropriate message for entering Vlad's tower.
- It looks like ice and venom got mixed up; cobras were spitting
  ice and white nagas were spitting venom.
- It might be simpler to just make the Punisher a ' rather than a `.
  After all, if a stone golem is pretty much just an animated statue,
  it would seem to fit the Punisher too.
- Crystal ice golems are kind of like the mumaks of the late game:
  dangerous if you allow them to get close to you, but easy enough
  to deal with once you know how to do so.  Their very high max
  HP makes it an exercise in tedium, though.  I would suggest that
  they be given half -- or less -- of the HP that they currently
  have. 
- Light sources seem to act strangely when you're over the water in
  the sheol-mid level -- not sure if this is a bug in the new code
  or not.  (You end up with a single-square vision radius even when
  carrying a lit lamp.)
- The Executioner managed to kill me the first time around (I killed
  it once, it was lifesaved and then I got stuck.)  Players will learn
  quickly enough to use other methods than melee to fight him.
- Blue slimes can freeze you in ice when you're levitating or water
  walking, both of which seem weird.

I can't really gauge the effect that it has on a real game since I
haven't played that way yet.  I've been playing the NetHack4 fork
recently ... any chance that you might port your code forward to that?

Stepping outside of the new branch, I would say that at least blue
slimes, black angels, and chillbugs would be interesting monsters to
add to vanilla.  I also like the new levels that are generated.

